WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:04.890
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.290
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.850
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。আর

4
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.110
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.270
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们要为你带来终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

6
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.770
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家访谈深入探索《办公室》的世界，

7
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.950
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
幕后花絮，以及大量的闺蜜故事。

8
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.990
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是“办公室女士 6.0”。

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.080
Hey there.
大家好。

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.040
Hi, everybody.
大家好，各位。

11
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.180
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

12
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.740
Happy Wednesday.
周三快乐。

13
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.260
How are you today?
你今天怎么样？

14
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.860
I'm good.
我很好。

15
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:34.620
Yeah.
对。

16
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:35.480
I'm feeling good.
我感觉很好。

17
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.380
Feeling good.
感觉不错。

18
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:36.860
Yeah.
对。

19
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.660
You know what I'm going to do later?
你知道我待会儿要做什么吗？

20
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:39.660
What?
做什么？

21
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.760
I am going to buy cheese at one of my favorite places to get cheese.
我要去我最喜欢的买奶酪的地方买奶酪。

22
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.180
Of all the things I thought you were going to say, that did not pop in my mind.
在我猜你想说的所有事情里，完全没有想到这个。

23
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.840
I love, I love a cheese board.
我爱，我太喜欢奶酪拼盘了。

24
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.020
Why are you making a cheese board?
你为什么要准备奶酪拼盘？

25
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.680
Because my sisters are visiting.
因为我的姐妹们要来拜访。

26
00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.140
Oh, okay.
哦，原来如此。

27
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.220
That's lovely.
太棒了。

28
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.000
I thought, you know, I want to set out a little something they can nibble on after a travel day.
我想，你知道的，她们舟车劳顿，我想准备点小点心让她们解解馋。

29
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.880
My new favorite snack is slices of brie cheese on these, like, seeded Trader Joe's crackers.
我最近最喜欢的零食是在那种有籽的乔氏超市饼干上放几片布里奶酪。

30
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.920
I mean, what's not to love?
我的意思是，谁能不爱呢？

31
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:14.540
I know.
我也觉得。

32
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.520
And then I'll put a few berries on the side.
然后我在旁边放几颗浆果。

33
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.060
This is my go-to snack.
这是我的首选小吃。

34
00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:18.960
On the side?
在旁边？

35
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.280
Why not put it right on top?
为什么不直接放在上面呢？

36
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:20.940
A berry?
浆果？

37
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.000
What was this reaction?
你这是什么反应？

38
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.400
A berry on top of some brie?
在布里奶酪上面放一颗浆果？

39
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.620
Am I saying something crazy here?
我说的话很疯狂吗？

40
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.060
An apple slice?
苹果片？

41
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.720
Like a green apple slice on top of your brie, on top of your cracker?
比如在你的饼干上、布里奶酪上放一片青苹果？

42
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.120
Sure.
当然可以。

43
00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:34.920
But a berry.
但如果是浆果的话。

44
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.600
Give me a raspberry on there.
给我来个覆盆子吧。

45
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.500
A raspberry?
覆盆子？

46
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.320
Why not?
为什么不呢？

47
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.920
Maybe a cranberry?
也许来点蔓越莓？

48
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.740
A lady.
真有品味。

49
00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:42.300
Come on.
拜托。

50
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.240
I eat cranberries and cheese all the time.
我经常吃蔓越莓配奶酪。

51
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:44.840
I brought some.
我带了一些。

52
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:45.540
Look, right here.
看，就在这儿。

53
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:46.820
Look at that.
快看那个。

54
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.840
Cranberries and cheese.
蔓越莓和奶酪。

55
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:48.960
Look at that.
快看那个。

56
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:52.220
Okay.
好啦。

57
00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.380
The sass we have started with this morning.
我们今天早上刚开始就这么傲娇。

58
00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:55.760
Okay.
好吧。

59
00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:56.820
From both of us.
我们两个都是。

60
00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.440
Let's tell everyone what we're doing today.
我们告诉大家今天要做什么吧。

61
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.840
Well, we have a really fun Office Lady 6.0.
嗯，我们有一期非常有趣的《办公室女士》6.0版。

62
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.900
We have not one, but two really fantastic guests on.
我们请来了不仅一位，而是两位非常棒的嘉宾。

63
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:07.680
We do.
没错。

64
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:15.160
We got to catch up with the amazing office writing team of Gene Stupnitsky and Lee Eisenberg.
我们得以和《办公室》里了不起的编剧团队吉娜·斯图普尼茨基和李·艾森伯格叙旧。

65
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.400
But before we get to those interviews, I was curious.
但在我们进入那些采访之前，我很好奇。

66
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.740
What were we doing, Jenna, in April 2008 on the set of The Office?
詹娜，2008年4月我们在《办公室》片场都在做什么？

67
00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:29.660
Because that is around the time when we filmed one of our guests today's most famous episodes.
因为那差不多就是我们拍摄今天其中一位嘉宾最著名的一集的时候。

68
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.420
And since I never delete an email, I can tell you.
既然我从不删邮件，我能告诉你。

69
00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:33.100
What?
什么？

70
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.300
This all centers around the week we were doing.
这一切都围绕着我们当时正在拍的那一周。

71
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.660
Can you guess it?
你能猜到吗？

72
00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.600
What is one of their most famous episodes?
他们最著名的一集是什么？

73
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.560
Their most famous episode is probably Dinner Party.
他们最著名的一集大概是《晚宴》。

74
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.140
Yes.
对。

75
00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.440
Dinner Party.
《晚宴》。

76
00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.580
First of all, I got an email from Joya at NBC.com.
首先，我收到了来自 NBC.com 的乔亚的一封邮件。

77
00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.900
She wrote me and said, hey, Angela, we saw some dailies from Dinner Party.
她写信对我说，嘿，安吉拉，我们看到了《晚宴》的一些样片。

78
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.540
That episode is going to be fantastic.
那一集会非常精彩。

79
00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.960
I can tell already.
我一眼就能看出来。

80
00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.180
I have some questions for you to answer.
我有一些问题需要你回答。

81
00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.620
Let me know if you can.
如果你能的话请告诉我。

82
00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:05.340
I responded, hey, we're on location the whole time at this condo, so no computer for me.
我回复说，嘿，我们这几天一直在那个公寓外景地拍戏，所以我碰不到电脑。

83
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.640
Can I do this next week?
我下周再做行吗？

84
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.880
Plus, we get home most nights at 10 p.m.
而且，我们那几周大部分晚上都是十点到家

85
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.020
and I go straight to bed.
然后直接上床睡觉。

86
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.800
So we were working some late nights that week.
所以那一周我们干得很晚。

87
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.300
I remember that.
我记得那个。

88
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.120
But next up, in my digital clutter, I got an email from you.
但接下来，在我的电子杂物堆里，我收到了你发的一封邮件。

89
00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.560
You were planning my baby shower.
你在筹备我的迎婴派对。

90
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.880
And I guess I had to come to set late because I had a doctor's appointment.
我猜我那天得晚点到片场，因为我有医生预约。

91
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.020
And you sent me an email titled, Tea Party!
你给我发了一封题为“茶会！”的邮件。

92
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.300
And when I opened it up, it said this.
当我打开它时，上面写着这个。

93
00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.140
Lady, you get your wish.
女士，你如愿以偿了。

94
00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.060
Your shower is going to be catered by Paddington's.
你的派对将由帕丁顿餐厅提供餐饮。

95
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:41.320
Oh, the best tea house in Los Angeles that has now shut down.
噢，洛杉矶最棒的茶馆，现在已经关门了。

96
00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:41.940
I know.
我知道。

97
00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.420
Oh, they had the best chicken salad tea sandwiches on this earth.
噢，他们家有这世上最好吃的鸡肉沙拉三明治。

98
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.260
It was so, it was just a cute little spot, too.
而且它真的很可爱，也是个温馨的小地方。

99
00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:49.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

100
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.760
And then you ended your email with, how big is the baby now?
然后你的邮件结尾是，现在宝宝有多大了？

101
00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:53.680
Oh.
哦。

102
00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.580
Next email was from Chris Haston, Kate's boyfriend.
下一封邮件来自克里斯·哈斯顿，凯特的男友。

103
00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:58.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

104
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.380
He was on the set of the dinner party taking pictures.
他在《晚宴》的片场拍照。

105
00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.040
And he sent me a really funny photo that he took of me and Rain between scenes in my big
他发给我一张非常搞笑的照片，是他拍的我跟雷恩在两场戏之间，

106
00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:07.700
preggers belly.
顶着我大大的孕肚。

107
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.140
He said, here's one.
他说，这是其中一张。

108
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.100
I've got some more.
我还有一些。

109
00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:10.920
Aw.
噢。

110
00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:11.500
Smiley face.
笑脸符号。

111
00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:12.740
And I have the picture.
然后我有这张照片。

112
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:13.360
Okay.
好的。

113
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.600
And, lady, you and I were doing press for the show.
然后，亲爱的，你和我当时在为这部剧做宣传。

114
00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.400
We got an email from NBC Publicity saying, we would like to do a satellite media tour with
我们收到了一封来自NBC宣传部的邮件，说，我们想和

115
00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.740
Jenna and Angela for the return of the show.
珍娜还有安吉拉一起做一个卫星媒体巡访，来迎接节目的回归。

116
00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.960
Oh, because it was the return after the big break of the writer's strike that year.
哦，因为那是当年编剧罢工大休假之后节目的回归。

117
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:31.300
Yeah.
对。

118
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.280
And it was going to be for dinner party.
而且即将播出的是《晚宴》那一集。

119
00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:33.920
Oh, boy.
噢，天哪。

120
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.840
You and I were going to start at 7 a.m.
你和我得从早上7点开始

121
00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.980
and go till 10 a.m.
一直聊到早上10点

122
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.040
talking about the show.
都在谈论这部剧。

123
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:38.520
Okay.
好吧。

124
00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.880
Next email was from me to you.
下一封邮件是我发给你的。

125
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.040
I guess your mom had sent me these fuzzy flip-flops.
我猜是你妈妈给我寄了这些毛茸茸的人字拖。

126
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:47.900
So I sent you a picture and I said, please pass this pic on to your mom.
所以我给你发了一张照片，并说，请把这张照片转交给你的妈妈。

127
00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.380
A thank you card is on the way.
感谢卡已经在路上了。

128
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.320
I love my flips.
我很喜欢我的拖鞋。

129
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.240
Oh.
哦。

130
00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.240
I was very pregnant in the picture.
照片里的我怀孕非常明显。

131
00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:57.000
Finally, Greg sent out an email to the cast and crew.
最后，格雷格给演职人员发了一封邮件。

132
00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.360
He said he would like to do a farewell for Kent Sabornak.
他说他想为肯特·萨博纳克举办一个欢送会。

133
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:05.540
Greg had gotten him a Rolex and had engraved on the back, Kent, good times.
格雷格给他买了一块劳力士，并在背面刻字：肯特，美好的时光。

134
00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.240
Love, the office.
爱你的，《办公室》剧组。

135
00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.540
Oh, that's so lovely.
哦，那太美好了。

136
00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.140
There's a little picture into our lives the week we filmed dinner party.
这就是我们拍摄《晚宴》那一周生活的缩影。

137
00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.980
Well, we talked to Jean and Lee a lot about dinner party.
我们和珍妮还有李聊了很多关于《晚宴》的事。

138
00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:17.540
We did.
确实如此。

139
00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.360
And it's a good convo.
这是一次很好的交流。

140
00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.940
They are so interesting to talk to.
跟他们聊天非常有意思。

141
00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.020
Their point of views about all of it.
他们对这一切的看法。

142
00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.020
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

143
00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:25.680
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

144
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.480
So, you guys, Jean and Lee joined The Office in season two and they wrote the biggest hit
所以，各位，珍妮和李是在第二季加入《办公室》的，他们写了这部剧最红的

145
00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.540
episodes of the show.
几集。

146
00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.480
That's right.
没错。

147
00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:39.560
They wrote The Fight, The Secret, Michael's Birthday, The Convention, Traveling Salesman,
他们写了《打架》、《秘密》、《迈克尔的生日》、《大会》、《出差推销员》、《回归》、《女性尊赏》以及《晚宴》、《招聘会》、《减肥》、《盈余》、《新老板》、《情人》、《托德·帕克》和《掩盖》。

148
00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:48.440
The Return, Women's Appreciation, and Dinner Party, Job Fair, Weight Loss, The Surplus,
他们还执导了《迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司》和《情人》。

149
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.960
New Boss, The Lover, Scott's Todds, and The Cover-Up.
新老板、情人、托德·帕克和掩盖。

150
00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:59.260
They also directed Michael Scott Paper Company and The Lover.
他们还执导了迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司和情人。

151
00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.060
And they made cameos as Gino and Leo from Vance Refrigeration.
他们还在《办公室》里客串出演了万斯冷气公司的吉诺和利奥。

152
00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.100
And, you know, in addition to their work on The Office, they also co-created, wrote,
而且，你知道，除了参与制作《办公室》，他们还共同创作、编剧

153
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:13.100
and executive produced HBO's Hello, Ladies with Stephen Merchant.
并执行监制了斯蒂芬·莫昌特在HBO推出的《你好，女士们》。

154
00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:13.820
It's great.
真的很棒。

155
00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.180
Yeah.
对啊。

156
00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.980
And they worked on other series like Trophy Wife.
他们还参与过其他剧集的制作，比如《特工老妈》。

157
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:22.720
They worked on Bad Teacher, both the movie and the television show, and Smilf.
他们参与过《坏老师》电影版和电视剧版，还有《驻店社畜》。

158
00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:27.700
And look, they've gone on both to be showrunners and written on several TV shows and movies
而且你看，他们后来都担任过剧集运作人，并各自

159
00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.780
separately, but they reunited in 2023 to co-create Jury Duty.
在多部电视剧和电影中担任编剧，但在2023年他们再度聚首，共同创作了《陪审义务》。

160
00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:33.760
Oh, it's so good.
哦，真的太好看了。

161
00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:34.760
It's so good.
真的太好看了。

162
00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.800
It's a critically acclaimed miniseries.
这是一部备受好评的迷你剧。

163
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:41.940
It won a Peabody Award for its innovative blend of comedy and reality storytelling.
它因创新融合了喜剧与真人秀叙事而荣获皮博迪奖。

164
00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.280
Well, listen, we just love this interview.
好了，听着，我们真的很喜欢这次采访。

165
00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:46.580
We kind of just went through their episodes.
我们基本上就是回顾了他们的剧集。

166
00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:51.460
And we also got some new insights into how the writing process worked on the show.
而且我们还对这部剧的编剧过程有了新的见解。

167
00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.200
So let's take a quick break.
那我们先休息一下。

168
00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.100
And when we come back, it's Gene and Lee.
等我们回来，就是吉恩和李了。

169
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:04.650
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请WDNC所有新老会员注意。

170
00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.530
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

171
00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:12.730
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年才发现，自己真的已经没那么多所谓了。

172
00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:18.390
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理清潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、不让人省心的

173
00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.810
families, brain fog, and bat wings.
家人、脑雾以及拜拜肉。

174
00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.690
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听见。

175
00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.590
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

176
00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:30.390
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get
在各大播客平台关注并收听由梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们不在乎俱乐部”

177
00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:31.150
your podcaSt.
播客。

178
00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.270
Gene and Lee.
吉恩和李。

179
00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:37.950
Hey, guys.
嘿，伙计们。

180
00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:38.730
Hello.
你们好。

181
00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:40.990
Welcome to Office, ladies.
欢迎来到《办公室女士》。

182
00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.870
We're so thrilled to have you here today.
我们非常高兴今天能邀请到二位。

183
00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.830
This is so fun.
这真的太有趣了。

184
00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.110
And Gene, I haven't seen you in forever.
吉恩，我好久没见你了。

185
00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:51.470
Lee, the last time I saw you, we ran into each other at the same dinner spot.
李，我上次见你，还是我们在同一家餐厅偶遇的时候。

186
00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:51.910
That was right.
没错。

187
00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:53.190
Years ago.
那是好几年前了。

188
00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:54.610
A lovely, lovely meetup.
一次非常美好温馨的相聚。

189
00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:56.710
I haven't seen you guys in so long.
我真的好久没见你们了。

190
00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.730
I mean, Lee, I do have a nuve bed cover on my bed.
我是说，李，我的床上的确铺着一张nuve床罩。

191
00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:00.650
We'll get to that.
我们等会儿会聊到这个。

192
00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:02.010
I'm very excited to discuss.
我很期待能讨论一下。

193
00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:03.050
That you sent me.
那是你送给我的。

194
00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:06.270
And Gene, I said this before we got on the mic.
吉恩，我在开麦前就说过这个。

195
00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.670
You look exactly the same to me.
在我看来你一点都没变。

196
00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.910
So I don't know what kind of magic potion.
所以我不知道你喝了什么神奇的魔药。

197
00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:11.930
Bless your heart.
你真好。

198
00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.170
It's called a filter.
这叫开滤镜了。

199
00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.030
That's my line.
那是我的台词。

200
00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.450
I was called a filter.
我刚才说的是开滤镜。

201
00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.830
Jenna, why don't you kick us off with the first question?
珍娜，要不你来抛砖引玉，问第一个问题？

202
00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:23.250
Well, you know, we normally ask people how they got their job on The Office.
好的，你知道的，我们通常会问别人是怎么得到《办公室》这份工作的。

203
00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.270
And that is one of our questions.
这也是我们的问题之一。

204
00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:30.170
But we want to back it up and ask, how did you two meet and become writing partners?
但我们想倒回前面，问一下，你们俩是怎么认识并成为编剧搭档的？

205
00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:31.570
Gene, you want to take this?
吉恩，你想接这个话吗？

206
00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:37.550
We met on the, not on the set, but on the office of the film Be Dazzled, Harold Ramis,
我们是在电影《神鬼愿望》的办公室里认识的，不是在片场，导演是哈罗德·雷米斯，

207
00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.470
who was a director, obviously, on The Office as well.
显然，他后来也是《办公室》的导演。

208
00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.850
And Lee was an office PA.
当时李是个办公室制片助理。

209
00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.390
And I was an intern.
而我是一个实习生。

210
00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:46.970
I had just moved to LA.
我刚搬到洛杉矶。

211
00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.470
And I think we had just moved to LA a few months before that.
我想我们也是在那之前几个月刚搬到洛杉矶的。

212
00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.550
And we became friends.
然后我们就成了朋友。

213
00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.650
And we didn't immediately start writing together.
我们并没有马上开始合作写剧本。

214
00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:55.930
But we were friends.
但我们是朋友。

215
00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:58.390
And we both wanted to be writers.
而且我们俩都想当编剧。

216
00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:01.150
I think, Lee, you were writing drama at the time, right?
我想，李，你当时在写正剧对吧？

217
00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:01.610
I was.
是的。

218
00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:03.470
I was writing very serious drama at the time.
我当时在写非常严肃的正剧。

219
00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:05.390
Very serious drama.
非常严肃的正剧。

220
00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:06.610
Please elaborate.
请详细说说。

221
00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.410
There's a little drama that's very serious.
就是那种很严肃的小正剧。

222
00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.750
Give us a nugget.
透露点干货吧。

223
00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.930
The first show that I ever got hired on was JAG.
我受雇的第一部剧是《执法悍将》。

224
00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.170
The military courtroom drama.
那个军事法庭题材的正剧。

225
00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:16.130
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

226
00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.370
That's pretty serious drama.
那确实是挺严肃的正剧。

227
00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.370
That is.
确实是。

228
00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:19.330
High stakes.
赌注很高。

229
00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.870
And then I was fired, I think, like, maybe four weeks in.
然后我想我大概第四周就被炒了。

230
00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.150
Maybe six weeks in.
也许是第六周。

231
00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.210
Were you given a reason for your firing?
他们给你开除的理由了吗？

232
00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.110
Were you just not dramatic?
是因为你不够戏剧化吗？

233
00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:32.730
Where to begin?
这让我从何说起呢？

234
00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.710
Well, I was so intimidated by, I was like,
嗯，我当时太怯场了，我在想，

235
00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.390
how do these people write, like, military courtroom stuff?
这些人怎么写得出那种军事法庭的东西？

236
00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:42.450
Like, so I basically just, like, Googled all, like, the acronyms
所以基本上，我把所有的缩写都百度了一遍，

237
00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.410
so that, like, my scripts would look like, you know,
这样我的剧本看起来就会显得，你知道的，

238
00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.450
that I, like, was in the military and had been a lawyer in the military.
就好像我当过兵，而且在部队里当过律师一样。

239
00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.670
And then the first note I got was, like, they couldn't follow anything
然后我收到的第一条意见就是，他们完全看不懂，

240
00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.990
because, like, I had all these acronyms that they didn't know existed.
因为我用了所有他们根本不知道存在的缩写。

241
00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:59.430
It was not a, respectfully, to anyone who worked on that show,
客观地说，并非针对任何曾在那部剧工作过的人，

242
00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.130
I did not find it.
我并没有觉得它……

243
00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:02.370
Now, with, like, the benefit of hindsight,
现在回想起来，

244
00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:03.910
it was not a particularly well-run show.
那并不是一部运营得特别好的剧。

245
00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:07.350
I don't think it really supported or lifted up young voices.
我觉得它并没有真正支持或提携年轻的声音。

246
00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.870
And also, to be fair to them,
而且，公平地说，

247
00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:12.570
I probably was not quite the right fit for it
考虑到我从那时起后来的职业发展，

248
00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.950
based on where my career went from there, from that moment.
我可能确实不太适合那部剧。

249
00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:16.350
Yes.
是的。

250
00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:16.950
Yeah.
对。

251
00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.190
So you guys started writing together
所以你们开始一起写作

252
00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:23.630
and was The Office your first job as writing partners?
《办公室》是你们作为编剧搭档的第一份工作吗？

253
00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:27.890
We sold a pilot to Fox a few months before we got on The Office
我们在加入《办公室》几个月前向福克斯卖出了一部试播集

254
00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.230
and that became our sample that Greg read
那成了格雷格读到的作品样品

255
00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:33.430
and Terry Weinberg and all the, you know,
还有特里·温伯格以及所有那些，你知道的，

256
00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:34.650
all the folks at Reveille had read.
Reveille的所有人都读过。

257
00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:39.330
And that was basically, we decided to write a show loosely based on us
基本上那是我们决定写一部大致根据我们自己改编的剧

258
00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:43.070
and we decided to not make it characters named Lee and Gene
我们决定不把角色命名为李和吉恩

259
00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:46.630
who were losers who lived together, who were codependent writers.
他们是住在一起、互为依附的失败编剧。

260
00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:50.910
So we basically took all of that except change their names to Lonnie and Gordo
所以我们基本上采用了所有这些，只是把他们的名字改成了隆尼和戈多

261
00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:52.450
and made them magicians.
并把他们设定为魔术师。

262
00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:53.830
But everything else was the same.
但其他一切都一样。

263
00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.850
They were codependent losers who lived together.
他们是住在一起、互为依附的失败者。

264
00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:00.230
And that became a sample that got us hired on The Office.
那成了让我们被《办公室》录用的作品样品。

265
00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.730
And maybe also became Leo and Gino.
可能也变成了莱奥和基诺。

266
00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.930
So we don't have a lot of range.
所以我们没有太多的戏路。

267
00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.630
It goes from Lee and Gene to Lonnie and Gordo to Leo and Gio.
从李和吉恩到隆尼和戈多，再到莱奥和吉奥。

268
00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.710
So when you guys came in to meet on The Office,
所以当你们来参加《办公室》的会面时，

269
00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:12.910
did you meet with Greg?
你们见到了格雷格吗？

270
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.970
Because a lot of people have shared with us their first meetings with Greg.
因为很多人跟我们分享过他们与格雷格的第一次会面。

271
00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.810
And I'm so curious if you had one.
我很好奇你们是不是也有过这样的经历。

272
00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:18.750
We did.
我们有。

273
00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.510
We met with Terry first and then we met with Greg
我们先见了特里，然后见了格雷格

274
00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.690
and we met him in like Westwood, I think.
我想我们是在韦斯特伍德那边见的面。

275
00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:24.410
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

276
00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:25.530
Like a coffee shop in Westwood.
就像韦斯特伍德的一家咖啡馆。

277
00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.910
And in my mind, I didn't know what he looked like,
在我脑海里，我不知道他长什么样，

278
00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.510
but I thought he'd be wearing a cowboy hat.
但我以为他会戴着牛仔帽。

279
00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.210
I think because of King of the Hill or something.
我想可能是因为《山丘之王》之类的原因吧。

280
00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:31.870
I don't know why.
我不知道为什么。

281
00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:35.170
I was like, he doesn't look anything like what I expect him to look like.
当时我想，他长得跟我预期的完全不一样。

282
00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:38.230
And our agent told us, you know, it'll probably be a long meeting.
我们的经纪人告诉我们，你知道的，这可能会是一场很长的会面。

283
00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.370
He does long meetings.
他总是开很长时间的会。

284
00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:40.510
And it was.
确实如此。

285
00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.470
It was a couple hours, two to three hours.
有好几个小时，两到三个小时。

286
00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:45.150
That is what we have heard from folks.
这就是我们从其他人那里听说的。

287
00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.030
And that the conversation goes kind of all over the place.
而且谈话内容可以说是天马行空、无所不包。

288
00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:48.830
Yeah.
对。

289
00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.390
No, he's I mean, he's very thoughtful.
不，他，我的意思是，他非常周到细致。

290
00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.950
You got a sense of how his brain worked.
你能感受到他的大脑是如何运转的。

291
00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:53.750
And, you know, nothing gets past him.
而且，你知道的，什么都逃不过他的眼睛。

292
00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.510
And he has a lot of questions.
他有很多问题。

293
00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.150
Yeah, it was something we had heard.
对，这是我们听说过的。

294
00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.710
And like, we kind of parroted it, parroted it.
然后我们有点像，学着鹦鹉学舌那样复述了它。

295
00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.250
And Greg got really excited.
格雷格变得非常兴奋。

296
00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:11.970
And and he's like, look, I just wrote that in my notebook right from theme.
然后他就像是，看，我刚刚就从主题里把那个写在我的笔记本上了。

297
00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:13.530
I remember that.
我记得那个。

298
00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:13.990
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

299
00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:14.950
It was actually like his notebook.
其实就像是他的笔记本一样。

300
00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:18.370
His notebook was like, it's what I imagine the Unabomber's notebook would have looked like.
他的笔记本看起来就像，我想象中的大学炸弹客的笔记本那种样子。

301
00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:21.190
It was really like every page was just filled.
真的就像每一页都写得满满当当的。

302
00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:25.010
Harold and and Harold Ramis had always talked about writing from theme.
哈罗德和哈罗德·雷米斯以前总是谈论从主题出发进行创作。

303
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:29.650
Gene and I, I would say, had not up until that point written from theme.
吉恩和我，我得说，在那之前并没有从主题出发进行过创作。

304
00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.190
And so he's like, what did you learn from Harold Ramis?
所以他就问，你从哈罗德·雷米斯那里学到了什么？

305
00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.750
I was like, what did we learn from Harold?
我就想，我们从哈罗德那里学到了什么？

306
00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.590
Like, I was like, how to smoke weed?
比如，我当时想，怎么抽大麻吗？

307
00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.930
Like, I like I was.
就像，我当时就是这么想的。

308
00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.590
And I said, I said, Harold always writes from theme.
然后我说，我说，哈罗德总是从主题出发进行创作。

309
00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.650
And Greg's eyes lit up.
格雷g的眼睛顿时亮了起来。

310
00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:48.250
And then he flipped to the page and in all block letters on the top, it said, theme is important.
接着他翻到那一页，上面顶端用全大写字母写着：主题很重要。

311
00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:49.450
Yeah.
是啊。

312
00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.130
Which I think is a very funny thing to see.
我觉得看到这个真的非常搞笑。

313
00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.290
Can you share with our listeners?
你能跟我们的听众分享一下吗？

314
00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:55.890
What does it mean to write from theme?
从主题出发创作是什么意思？

315
00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:01.110
Writing from theme is like you want to explore jealousy.
从主题出发创作就像是你想探讨嫉妒。

316
00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:03.510
You want to explore a mother daughter dynamic.
你想探讨母女关系。

317
00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.790
You know, it's the haves and the have nots.
你知道的，这就是富人和穷人的区别。

318
00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:10.710
It's kind of like writing from an idea and writing from character.
这有点像从一个理念出发创作，以及从人物出发创作。

319
00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:16.190
Be like, oh, I think it'd be really funny if there was a character who was the manager of an office.
就像是，哦，我觉得如果有一个角色是办公室经理，那一定会非常搞笑。

320
00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.430
And then he could be funny because of X, Y, and Z.
然后他可以因为各种原因而变得很好笑。

321
00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:21.730
I would say Seinfeld has no theme.
我要说《宋飞传》就没有主题。

322
00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:24.430
Seinfeld is just purely character comedy.
《宋飞传》纯粹是人物喜剧。

323
00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:25.630
Okay.
好吧。

324
00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:27.630
That is so interesting to me.
这对我来说太有趣了。

325
00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.110
And it made it into Greg's book.
而且它还被收录进了格雷g的书里。

326
00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:31.390
His spiral that he carries around.
就是他随身携带的那本螺旋装订笔记本。

327
00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:34.690
But then you guys actually joined the staff in season two.
但后来你们俩确实在第二季加入了编剧团队。

328
00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:35.570
Right.
没错。

329
00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.110
Yeah.
是啊。

330
00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:42.070
I mean, we were, when we were living together, we would, first we watched the British office and we were huge fans of that.
我是说，我们，当我们住在一起的时候，我们，首先我们看了英版《办公室》，我们是它的超级粉丝。

331
00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.870
And then we saw season one and we were huge fans of that.
然后我们看了第一季，我们也是它的超级粉丝。

332
00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.850
We were really impressed at how you guys pulled it off because we did not, like everyone else,
我们对你们是如何成功驾驭它的感到非常印象深刻，因为我们没有，和所有人一样，

333
00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:55.050
we did not have high expectations for the American version because we love the British one so much.
我们对美版并没有抱太高的期望，因为我们太喜欢英版了。

334
00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:56.330
And how could it be good?
而且它怎么可能会好看呢？

335
00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.650
And we saw the pilot actually, right?
而且我们其实看过试播集，对吧？

336
00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:00.210
Yeah.
对。

337
00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:01.410
The pilot.
试播集。

338
00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.410
And not even like the final cut.
而且甚至还不是最终剪辑版。

339
00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:05.310
We had a friend who worked at NBC who showed us the pilot.
我们有个在NBC工作的朋友给我们看了试播集。

340
00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.250
I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

341
00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:10.170
And then we watched the first season, you know, every week.
然后我们每周都看第一季。

342
00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.210
And it was like six episodes.
总共只有六集。

343
00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.750
And it was just fantastic.
而且简直太棒了。

344
00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:15.270
I mean, we couldn't believe it.
我是说，我们简直不敢相信。

345
00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:19.210
And then after we met with Greg, we got a call from our agent.
后来在跟格雷g见面之后，我们接到了经纪人的电话。

346
00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.810
And we were offered the office with no guarantee of that we'd be able to write a script.
我们得到了加入《办公室》的机会，但并不能保证我们一定能写剧本。

347
00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.210
Just, I think it was like eight episodes or something.
只是，我觉得大概是八集左右吧。

348
00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:29.370
It was six episodes for the office with like six backup scripts.
《办公室》只有六集，外加大概六个备用剧本。

349
00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:30.030
Yeah.
对。

350
00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:34.370
Like if you counted the number of writers, it felt like pretty, we were going to be one of the backup scripts.
如果你数一下编剧的人数，就会觉得，我们基本上就是去充当备用剧本的。

351
00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:35.070
Yeah.
是啊。

352
00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.390
And then, or a full season on an animated show on Fox, one of those animated shows.
然后呢，或者是福克斯电视台一部动画剧集的一整季，那种动画剧集之一。

353
00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:42.810
And American Dad, which has been on for 30 years.
还有《美国老爹》，已经播了30年了。

354
00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:48.570
So you had to pick American Dad, which had a long, long like shelf life possibilities, right?
所以你得选《美国老爹》，它有着很长很长的续播可能性，对吧？

355
00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:53.830
Or kind of take a risk on this show that only had a six episode pickup for the first season.
或者冒个险，选这部第一季只预定了六集的剧。

356
00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.770
And there was one more, well, there was one more show in the mix.
还有一个，嗯，候选里还有另一部剧。

357
00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:56.290
Do you remember, Gene?
你还记得吗，吉恩？

358
00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:58.190
Was it a John Stamos show?
是约翰·斯塔莫斯的剧吗？

359
00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.230
Jake in Progress.
《发展中的杰克》。

360
00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:00.150
That's right.
没错。

361
00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.250
With John Stamos.
由约翰·斯塔莫斯主演。

362
00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:02.830
That's right.
没错。

363
00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:03.110
Wow.
哇。

364
00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:04.010
Yeah.
是啊。

365
00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.630
Real sliding doors moment for us.
对我们来说真是个命运转折的时刻。

366
00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:06.890
You know, even though.
你知道的，尽管如此。

367
00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:10.790
But guys, you had three offers to choose from.
但是伙计们，你们当时有三个offer可以选。

368
00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:17.930
I mean, we know how talented you guys are, but that is not usual for writers to have like
我的意思是，我们知道你们很有才华，但编剧在新的电视季刚开始时能有

369
00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.590
three different job offers at the beginning of a new television season.
三份不同的工作邀请，这并不常见。

370
00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.090
That's kind of rad.
这简直太酷了。

371
00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.270
This was after five years of abject failure.
这是经历了五年的彻底失败之后的事。

372
00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.430
So, you know.
所以呢，你懂的。

373
00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.850
This was your year.
这是你们时来运转的一年。

374
00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:32.170
The year before we got hired on the office, and Gene, you can correct me on the number.
就在我们被《办公室》雇佣的前一年，吉恩，你可以纠正我的数字。

375
00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.070
And I don't like to talk about money because it's tacky.
而且我不喜欢谈论钱，因为那很俗气。

376
00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:40.250
But Gene declared, I believe, $8,000 in earnings the year before he was hired on the office.
但吉恩宣称，我相信，在他被《办公室》雇佣的前一年，他的收入是8000美元。

377
00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.450
Yeah, I think it was like $7,000.
对，我想大概是7000美元吧。

378
00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:42.250
Yeah.
是啊。

379
00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.270
But I remember my accountant was like, okay, let me get your tax returns from last year.
但我记得我的会计当时说，好吧，让我看看你去年的纳税申报表。

380
00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:46.830
I was like, taxes?
我当时想，报税？

381
00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:47.530
I was like, what do you mean?
我当时想，你什么意思？

382
00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:48.750
I was like, what?
我当时想，什么？

383
00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:49.870
There were big taxes.
那可是很大一笔税呢。

384
00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.930
And then so, you know, it was not even a question.
然后所以，你知道的，这根本不用考虑。

385
00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.410
Even though it was going to be a guaranteed full season of this other show that had been
尽管另一部剧已经播了很久，而且保证有一整季的预定，

386
00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.770
running for a long time, we didn't even hesitate.
但我们连犹豫都没犹豫。

387
00:15:58.970 --> 00:15:59.990
We knew we wanted to be on the office.
我们知道我们想去《办公室》。

388
00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.470
Even if it was only going to be six episodes.
哪怕它只有六集。

389
00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:02.630
It was a no-brainer.
这是毫无疑问的。

390
00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.630
And then your very first episode was the fight.
然后你们的第一集就是《打架》那一集。

391
00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:13.970
And, you know, I was looking up the best Jim Dwight pranks, and this opener is listed in
而且，你知道的，我查了吉姆和德怀特的最佳恶作剧，这个开场被列入了

392
00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:19.930
every list where people love this prank where Jim puts Dwight's desk in the bathroom.
每一个榜单里，大家都很喜欢吉姆把德怀特的办公桌搬到洗手间里的那个恶作剧。

393
00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.590
But it's so funny.
但它真的太搞笑了。

394
00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:22.430
Fans love it.
粉丝们都很喜欢。

395
00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:25.630
Time Magazine did a list of all the best Jim pranks.
《时代周刊》盘点过所有吉姆的最佳恶作剧。

396
00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:26.970
That one makes it on there.
那个恶作剧就榜上有名。

397
00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.950
What a fun episode to have be your first episode.
能让这样一集作为你们的第一集，真是有趣极了。

398
00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.130
It was, I actually just rewatched it, Gene.
确实，吉恩，我其实刚重温过一遍。

399
00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.330
It's really, I was really proud of it.
真的，我为它感到非常骄傲。

400
00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.790
It was really, it was very, it was fun.
真的很棒，非常有趣。

401
00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:40.710
It was so, you know, we wrote that episode, the entire first season of the, I would say
当时的情况就是，你知道的，我们写那一集时，整个第一季，我可以说

402
00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:45.630
like maybe the first season two, season three, I was convinced we were going to get fired.
大概第一季到第二季、第三季吧，我都确信我们会遭解雇。

403
00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:50.790
I think like probably until maybe like, maybe until dinner party, I thought like every,
我想可能大概直到，也许直到《晚宴》那一集，我都觉得每一个，

404
00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:52.590
and maybe even past dinner party.
甚至可能过了《晚宴》之后也是如此。

405
00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.410
I just, I was always waiting to be fired.
我只是，我总是在等着被炒鱿鱼。

406
00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:55.350
Gene was too.
吉恩也是。

407
00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:58.810
And so when we wrote the fight, Greg had pneumonia.
所以当我们写《争吵》那集时，格雷格得了肺炎。

408
00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:02.670
And so everyone kind of got sent off to write their scripts.
然后大家都各自被派去写自己的剧本。

409
00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:06.850
And we kind of like, we were sent off with like as little information as like one could
我们差不多就像是，带着极少的信息被派出去，少到一个人

410
00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.350
be sent off with to write an outline.
去写大纲时所能得到的最低限度。

411
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.730
And certainly for your first episode, it had kind of Jag vibes to it.
而且对你的第一集来说，它确实有点像《执法悍将》的风格。

412
00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:18.310
And, and so we wrote this outline and we went to Greg's house to get notes.
所以，我们写了这个大纲，然后去了格雷格家听取意见。

413
00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.370
Like, cause Greg couldn't come into the office.
因为格雷格不能来办公室。

414
00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.670
He was that sick.
他病得那么重。

415
00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:22.250
Yeah.
是啊。

416
00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.490
Pretending to be that sick.
装出病得那么重 हिसाब。

417
00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:24.290
Yeah, exactly.
对，没准。

418
00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:30.210
And so we went to Greg's house and I remember Greg teaching us about subtext because we,
所以我们去了格雷格家，我记得格雷格教我们什么是潜台词，因为我们，

419
00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:35.130
we were like, a bit like Jim and Pam, like Jim probably said something like, I really like
我们当时有点像吉姆和帕姆，吉姆大概说了诸如“我真的很喜欢

420
00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:35.370
you.
你”这样的话。

421
00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:38.270
He was like, Hey, you might want to dial that back.
他当时说，嘿，你可能得收敛一点。

422
00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:43.250
Sometimes when someone, you know, has an interest in someone else, they sometimes without saying
有时候当某人，你知道的，对另一个人有好感时，他们有时不用明说，

423
00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.670
it, you get a sense of how they feel.
你也能感觉到他们的心意。

424
00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:45.670
Oh, interesting.
哦，有意思。

425
00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:46.010
Okay.
好吧。

426
00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.290
That's why we're both single.
难怪我们俩都单身。

427
00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:51.490
And so then we were, and so then I was like, you can like someone and not tell them.
然后我们就觉得，原来你可以喜欢一个人却不告诉对方。

428
00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:55.270
And so, you know, we ended up doing a rewrite on the outline and ended up writing the first
所以，你知道的，我们最后对大纲进行了重写，并最终写出了第一版

429
00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:55.550
draft.
初稿。

430
00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:58.790
But the entire time I was like, Oh, they're setting us up to fail.
但在整个过程中我都觉得，天哪，他们这是在设局让我们失败。

431
00:17:59.070 --> 00:17:59.870
This is their excuse.
这就是他们的借口。

432
00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:01.450
We're going to write a terrible draft of the script.
我们要写出一版糟糕透顶的剧本初稿。

433
00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:04.650
And then everyone knows that we don't belong on the show and then we'll get fired.
然后所有人都会发现我们根本不配留在剧组，接着我们就会被开除。

434
00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.130
And then it was like, of course, that's like where things are headed.
当时就觉得，理所当然，事情就是朝着那个方向发展的。

435
00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:08.770
But that did not happen.
但那并没有发生。

436
00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:09.230
Did not happen.
并没有发生。

437
00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:10.370
The fight is awesome.
《争吵》那一集棒极了。

438
00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.390
And you guys wrote so many great episodes before dinner party.
而且在《晚宴》之前，你们俩就写了那么多精彩的剧集。

439
00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.310
Telling you, I'm letting you into our mind.
我跟你说，我这是在让你们走进我们的内心世界。

440
00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:16.030
Yeah.
是啊。

441
00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:20.390
I will say I wasn't as worried that we were going to get fired, but I do remember we wanted
不过我要说的是，我当时没那么担心会被开除，但我确实记得我们很早就想

442
00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.650
to leave the show early on.
离开这个剧组。

443
00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:23.250
And we called our agent.
我们给经纪人打了电话。

444
00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:24.530
We're like, we don't, we don't like it here.
我们说，我们不，我们不喜欢这里。

445
00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:25.650
We want to go.
我们要走。

446
00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:26.850
Everyone was mean to us.
每个人都对我们不好。

447
00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:28.890
And he's like, uh-huh.
然后他说，嗯哼。

448
00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:30.170
He's like, are you an idiot?
他说，你们是脑残吗？

449
00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.710
We had been offered a blind script by Fox.
福克斯曾向我们约过一份定向剧本。

450
00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:33.790
We sold that.
我们把它卖出去了。

451
00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:38.770
We sold Lottie and Gordo to Fox and they offer us a blind script, which means that, you
我们把《洛蒂和戈多》卖给了福斯，他们给我们提供了一份盲签剧本合约，也就是说，

452
00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:42.250
know, they would basically give us money without knowing what the idea was, but we'd
你知道的，他们基本上在不知道创意是什么的情况下就给我们钱，但我们

453
00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.430
have to come up with a story for them and a script.
必须为他们想出一个故事和一个剧本。

454
00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:47.590
And it was for a lot less money than working on the office.
而且这比在《办公室》工作赚的钱少得多。

455
00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.530
But yes, people were not nice to us initially.
但没错，一开始人们对我们并不友好。

456
00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.650
And we were intimidated.
而且我们感到很受威慑。

457
00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:51.910
We did ask if we could leave.
我们确实问过能不能离开。

458
00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.950
Who wasn't nice to you?
谁对你们不友好？

459
00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:56.290
Well, it's so ironic because the people who weren't nice to me.
嗯，这太讽刺了，因为那些对我不友好的人。

460
00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.950
Name the names or say departments.
说出名字或者说出部门。

461
